;; Configuration for the documentation site, read by the docs-engine
;; (https://github.com/jlt-commons/docs-engine).
;;
;; Build or preview it from this repo:
;;   bb site:build     generate _site/
;;   bb site:serve     build, then serve at localhost:3000
;;   bb site:clean     delete the build output
;;
;; NOTHING PUBLISHES. This repo is private, and no site repo, GitHub Pages
;; setting or S3 target is wired up for it. `bb site:build` writes to a local
;; directory that is gitignored, and that is the whole pipeline today. When
;; the repo goes public, the publish half gets added deliberately, as its own
;; change, the way the sibling raylib-pacman has it.
{;; :base-path is what makes this a project site rather than an org one. If it
 ;; is ever served at https://b12n-oss.github.io/lisp-games/, every URL the
 ;; engine emits needs that prefix. Leave it out and the pages still render,
 ;; but each one loads the ORGANIZATION site's stylesheet and every asset
 ;; 404s.
 :base-path   "/lisp-games"

 :title       "lisp-games"
 :description "Small graphical programs, each ported to more than one Clojure-family runtime, kept side by side so the differences are measurable rather than arguable."

 ;; The stills the guide pages link to.
 :asset-dirs  ["demos"]}
